C%20a%2022-year-old%20working%20in%20medical%20sales%20who%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmoved-to-new-york-for-job-gave-up-dream-home-2025-9%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3E%3Cem%3Emoved%20to%20New%20York%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cem%3E%20in%20June.%20The%20conversation%20has%20been%20edited%20for%20length%20and%20clarity.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20had%20just%20graduated%20from%20college%20and%20was%20moving%20from%20Massachusetts%20to%20New%20York%20for%20a%20job%20starting%20in%20June.%20I%20planned%20to%20get%20an%20apartment%20with%20friends%2C%20but%20they%20wouldn't%20arrive%20in%20the%20city%20until%20the%20end%20of%20July.%20Since%20they%20didn't%20want%20to%20start%20paying%20New%20York%20rent%20before%20they%20needed%20to%2C%20I%20had%20to%20find%20a%20short-term%20place%20to%20stay%20in%20the%20meantime.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EFinding%20long-term%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fnyc-housing-affordability-maps-renters-2026-4%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ehousing%20in%20New%20York%3C%2Fa%3E%20is%20already%20difficult%2C%20and%20looking%20for%20a%20short-term%20lease%20is%20even%20harder.%20I%20was%20in%20a%20time%20crunch%20and%20didn't%20really%20know%20where%20to%20start.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20wanted%20to%20live%20close%20to%20the%20hospital%20where%20I'd%20be%20working%20because%20I%20was%20new%20to%20the%20city%20and%20unfamiliar%20with%20public%20transportation.%20I%20was%20also%20just%20starting%20out%2C%20so%20I%20wanted%20something%20affordable%20that%20was%20still%20safe.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThere%20are%20a%20bunch%20of%20NYC%20Facebook%20groups%20where%20people%20post%20things%20like%2C%20%26quot%3BMy%20roommate%20just%20left%2C%20and%20we're%20looking%20for%20someone%20to%20fill%20their%20spot.%26quot%3B%20Those%20can%20be%20good%2C%20but%20you%20have%20to%20get%20lucky%20with%20the%20timing%20and%20location.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20also%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fairbnb-solo-travel-safety-tip-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Elooked%20on%20Airbnb%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20websites%20like%20SpareRoom%20and%20Furnished%20Finder.%20I%20reached%20out%20to%20a%20few%20people%2C%20but%20some%20of%20the%20situations%20were%20weird.%20It%20would%20be%20like%2C%20%26quot%3BMy%20cousin%20is%20sleeping%20on%20the%20couch%2C%26quot%3B%20or%2C%20%26quot%3BSomeone%20else%20might%20also%20be%20staying%20in%20the%20room.%26quot%3B%20So%20I%20avoided%20those.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EEventually%2C%20I%20found%20a%20listing%20from%20a%2070-year-old%20woman%20named%20Aleyda%20on%20SpareRoom.%20We%20messaged%20a%20little%2C%20and%20I%20figured%20she%20was%20probably%20a%20safer%20bet.%20It%20was%20an%20unusual%20living%20arrangement%2C%20but%20I%20decided%20to%20take%20a%20chance.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22ff609a54-4d80-442f-a575-2c3c64397820%5C%22%3EI%20took%20a%20risk%2C%20and%20it%20was%20worth%20it%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EI%20FaceTimed%20Aleyda%20to%20see%20the%20apartment%2C%20but%20the%20person%20I%20spoke%20with%20wasn't%20even%20her.%20It%20was%20a%20younger%20guy%20who%20lived%20in%20the%20building%20and%20was%20helping%20translate%20for%20her%20because%20she%20spoke%20Spanish.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EHe%20showed%20me%20around%20the%20apartment%2C%20and%20I%20liked%20it.%20Still%2C%20I%20was%20a%20little%20suspicious%20because%20I%20thought%2C%20%26quot%3BI'm%20not%20even%20meeting%20the%20person%20I'm%20going%20to%20be%20living%20with.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20told%20my%20parents.%20My%20dad%2C%20who's%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmoved-from-boston-area-to-upstate-new-york-pros-cons-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Efrom%20Boston%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20was%20basically%20like%2C%20%26quot%3BYeah%2C%20you'll%20be%20fine.%26quot%3B%20My%20mom%20was%20more%20concerned.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBeing%20a%20guy%20made%20it%20feel%20a%20little%20less%20scary.%20So%20I%20decided%20to%20go%20for%20it%20and%20hope%20the%20apartment%20actually%20existed.%20Worst%20case%2C%20I%20figured%20I'd%20get%20a%20hotel%20or%20find%20something%20else.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%224284%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22A%20person%20stands%20near%20hanging%20clothes%20in%20a%20narrow%20empty%20room%20with%20wood%20flooring%20and%20luggage.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7611a48fcc2e955f7de6a5%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%223213%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3ESwanson%20in%20his%20NYC%20bedroom%20in%20the%20apartment%20that%20he%20shared%20with%20Aleyda.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20William%20Swanson%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EOn%20move-in%20day%2C%20I%20finally%20met%20Aleyda%20and%20was%20relieved%20to%20find%20out%20she%20was%20a%20real%20person%20and%20I%20wasn't%20getting%20scammed.%20My%20parents%20helped%20me%20move%20in%20because%20they%20wanted%20to%20meet%20her%2C%20too.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShe%20was%20incredibly%20nice%20and%20caring.%20I%20remember%20my%20mom%20was%20taken%20aback%20by%20how%20lucky%20I%20had%20gotten.%20I%20had%20somehow%20found%20the%20perfect%20roommate.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%228bf3aa35-1d99-4b45-9d49-f03ae816e40e%5C%22%3EWe%20had%20an%20unusual%20but%20great%20living%20arrangement%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EI%20don't%20know%20too%20much%20about%20Aleyda%20because%20I%20didn't%20want%20to%20ask%20her%20too%20many%20questions.%20What%20I%20do%20know%20is%20that%20I%20was%20the%2011th%20or%2012th%20person%20she%20had%20rented%20the%20room%20to.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAleyda's%20apartment%20has%20three%20bedrooms%2C%20a%20kitchen%2C%20and%20a%20small%20living%20room.%20She%20sleeps%20in%20one%20bedroom%2C%20another%20is%20used%20for%20storage%2C%20and%20mine%20was%20near%20the%20bathroom%20we%20shared.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20paid%20about%20%241%2C900%20for%20the%20month%20without%20utilities%2C%20which%20is%20objectively%20insane.%20But%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fairbnb-host-how-to-select-a-short-term-rental-property-2025-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eshort-term%20rentals%3C%2Fa%3E%20are%20more%20expensive%2C%20and%20it%20was%20still%20one%20of%20the%20better%20deals%20I%20could%20find%20in%20a%20great%20location.%20I%20figured%20I'd%20eat%20the%20cost%20for%20a%20month.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAleyda%20speaks%20Spanish%2C%20so%20a%20lot%20of%20the%20time%20we%20texted%2C%20and%20I%20think%20she%20used%20some%20kind%20of%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flanguage-translator-uses-ai-wont-replace-adapt-2024-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EAI%20to%20help%20with%20translation%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20also%20have%20a%20Colombian%20friend%20who%20speaks%20Spanish%2C%20so%20sometimes%20I'd%20FaceTime%20him%20to%20help%20us%20communicate.%20Other%20times%2C%20the%20neighbor%20would%20help.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIt%20was%20obviously%20a%20nontraditional%20living%20situation%20%E2%80%94%20a%2022-year-old%20guy%20living%20with%20a%2070-year-old%20woman%20%E2%80%94%20but%20she%20was%20super%20laid-back%20and%20let%20me%20do%20my%20own%20thing.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShe%20had%20a%20few%20rules%3A%20no%20partying%2C%20drugs%2C%20drinking%2C%20or%20having%20a%20bunch%20of%20people%20over.%20Basically%2C%20she%20was%20like%2C%20%26quot%3BWhatever%20you%20do%20outside%20my%20apartment%2C%20I%20can't%20control.%26quot%3B%20I%20thought%20that%20was%20fair.%20I%20was%20coming%20into%20her%20home%2C%20so%20I%20was%20going%20to%20play%20by%20her%20rules.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAleyda%20had%20a%20social%20life%20of%20her%20own.%20She%20was%20always%20out%20with%20friends.%20Sometimes%20she'd%20make%20me%20meals%2C%20and%20I'd%20ask%20her%20to%20eat%20with%20me%2C%20but%20she'd%20be%20like%2C%20%26quot%3BNo%2C%20I'm%20busy.%20I%20have%20somewhere%20to%20go%2C%20but%20please%20eat.%26quot%3B%20Some%20nights%2C%20she'd%20stay%20up%20watching%20TV%20way%20later%20than%20I%20did%2C%20which%20was%20kind%20of%20funny.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%224284%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22A%20plate%20o