2Fmens-gym-essentials-workout-clothing-gear-fitness-tech-2025-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EAthletic%20shorts%20with%20five-inch%20inseams%3C%2Fa%3E%20won't%20cut%20it%2C%20and%20neither%20will%20satin%2C%20lace-lined%20bottoms.%20That%20means%20this%20isn't%20the%20time%20to%20try%20those%20extra-short%20styles%20loved%20by%20Paul%20Mescal%20and%20Harry%20Styles%2C%20nor%20the%20daring%20pairs%20worn%20by%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Fp%2FDJ_xWVSC8eo%2F%3Futm_source%3Dig_web_copy_link%26igsh%3DNTc4MTIwNjQ2YQ%3D%3D%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EAlexander%20Skarsg%C3%A5rd%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BIf%20a%20skirt%20of%20the%20same%20length%20would%20be%20too%20short%2C%20you%20shouldn't%20be%20wearing%20those%20shorts%2C%26quot%3B%20Waliji%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%225584%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Men%20wear%20two%20different%20styles%20of%20shorts%20with%20ankle%20socks%20and%20loafers.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a75e7b98fcc2e955f7de4a7%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%224188%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EThe%20shorts%20on%20the%20left%20wouldn't%20be%20work%20appropriate%2C%20but%20the%20shorts%20on%20the%20right%20would.%3Cp%3EEdward%20Berthelot%2FGetty%20Images%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EInstead%2C%20Waliji%20said%20workers%20should%20generally%20stick%20to%20trouser-style%20shorts%20and%20long%20chinos.%20Sorry%20to%20fans%2C%20but%20this%20rules%20out%20denim%20and%20cargo%20shorts.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBold%20colors%2C%20however%2C%20are%20fine%20%E2%80%94%20if%20they're%20styled%20nicely.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BA%20red%20short%20with%20a%20white%20button-down%20shirt%20and%20loafers%20would%20look%20nice%2C%26quot%3B%20Waliji%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShe%20also%20recommends%20elevating%20shorts%20by%20pairing%20them%20with%20more%20formal%20tops%2C%20like%20polo%20shirts%2C%20and%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fguides%2Fstyle%2Fbest-loafers-men%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eclassic%20accessories%20like%20loafers%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20leather%20belts.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EUltimately%2C%20as%20long%20as%20you%20dress%20respectfully%20and%20modestly%20%E2%80%94%20as%20you%20likely%20would%20with%20any%20work%20outfit%20%E2%80%94%20Waliji%20said%20you'll%20be%20fine.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BIt%20all%20depends%20on%20where%20you're%20working%20and%20your%20dress%20code%2C%26quot%3B%20Waliji%20said.%20%26quot%3BIf%20you're%20an%20attorney%2C%20you%20need%20to%20be%20in%20a%20suit.%20I%20don't%20think%20a%20blazer%20and%20shorts%20are%20going%20to%20work.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhow-to-wear-shorts-to-work-office-stylist-advice-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786193881000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a75d9660c0bf4e8be522971%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fhow-to-wear-shorts-to-work-office-stylist-advice-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22Instagram%20head%20Adam%20Mosseri%20said%20he's%20%26quot%3Bpro%26quot%3B%20wearing%20shorts%20at%20the%20office.%20A%20stylist%20told%20us%20how%20to%20wear%20them%20and%20still%20look%20professional.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22akrause%40businessinsider.com%20(Amanda%20Krause)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22I%20dreaded%20raising%205%20teens%20under%20one%20roof.%20Then%20they%20all%20started%20becoming%20people%20I'd%20love%20to%20hang%20out%20with.%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%226720%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22A%20family%20is%20shown%20from%20behind%20with%20their%20arms%20wrapped%20around%20each%20other.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a75ecad0c6c5a263f3a77f0%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%224480%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EThe%20author%20(not%20pictured)%20said%20she's%20enjoying%20parenting%20during%20the%20teen%20years%20more%20than%20she%20expected%20to.%3Cp%3ERealPeopleGroup%2FGetty%20Images%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3ETeens%20and%20tweens%20have%20a%20bad%20reputation%2C%20and%20some%20of%20it%20is%20deserved.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EBut%20there's%20another%20side%20to%20parenting%20teens%20that%20people%20don't%20often%20share.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EI%20love%20seeing%20the%20people%20they%20are%20becoming%20and%20hanging%20out%20with%20kids%20I%20truly%20enjoy%20being%20around.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EThink%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fparents-say-teens-tough-love-raising-high-school-kids-2025-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eraising%20one%20teenager%3C%2Fa%3E%20is%20difficult%3F%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EImagine%20living%20with%20five.%20That's%20where%20I'll%20be%20in%20two%20years'%20time%20when%20my%20youngest%20two%20join%20their%20older%20siblings%20in%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flessons-ive-learned-from-parenting-four-teens-2024-12%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Edreaded%20teenage%20years%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20you%20know%20what%3F%20I'm%20looking%20forward%20to%20it%20more%20than%20you'd%20think.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22fa77310e-5b44-4210-a489-85266c98ac0a%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3ETeens%20get%20a%20bad%20rap%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EI%20get%20it.%20Teenagers%20have%20a%20bad%20reputation%2C%20and%20raising%20them%20can%20be%20challenging.%20But%20stand%20by%20for%20a%20controversial%20opinion%3A%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fno-one-taught-me-how-to-parent-a-teenager-2025-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eliving%20with%20teens%3C%2Fa%3E%20can%20also%20be%20a%20lot%20of%20fun.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EYes%2C%20I'll%20probably%20never%20be%20able%20to%20buy%20enough%20snacks%20to%20satisfy%20them%2C%20and%20I%20don't%20doubt%20I'll%20be%20removing%20more%20than%20my%20share%20of%20festering%20food%20bowls%20from%20stinky%20rooms.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%224054%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22The%20author%2C%20GILLIAN%20HARVEY.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a75ea8b0c0bf4e8be522a71%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%226001%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EThe%20author%20said%20she's%20enjoying%20having%20multiple%20teens%20in%20her%20house%20more%20than%20she%20expected%20to.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20Gillian%20Harvey.%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EI%20also%20expect%20my%20fair%20share%20of%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fteen-was-pushing-the-boundaries-a-trip-reset-our-relationship-2025-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eteenage%20boundary%20pushing%3C%2Fa%3E%20as%20my%20kids%20begin%20to%20morph%20into%20the%20adults%20they'll%20become.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20kids%20already%20have%20moments%20where%20they%20find%20constant%20fault%20with%20their%20mom%2C%20everything%20from%20my%20cooking%20to%20the%20standard%20of%20my%20cleaning%20(this%20from%20kids%20who%20use%20an%20entire%20room%20as%20a%20floordrobe).%20Oh%2C%20and%20I'm%20officially%20%26quot%3Bso%20embarrassing.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22599007ab-b95a-4d2e-b65f-6ab74a67be9b%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EThere's%20a%20good%20side%20to%20raising%20teens%2C%20too%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EAlongside%20the%20hair-tearing%20(mine)%20and%20the%20complaining%20(theirs)%2C%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Ftrader-joes-favorite-things-busy-parent-teens-meals-snacks-2023-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eexcessive%20eating%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20reluctance%20to%20do%20homework%2C%20there's%20quite%20a%20lot%20of%20joy%20to%20be%20found%20in%20raising%20teens.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ETake%20my%20daughter%2C%20for%20example.%20Two%20years%20ago%2C%20she%20pretty%20much%20hated%20everything%20about%20me.%20But%20at%2016%2C%20she's%20emerged%20from%20her%20hormonal%20chrysalis%20and%20become%20a%20lovely%20young%20woman.%20We%20talk%2C%20almost%20as%20equals.%20We%20make%20each%20other%20laugh.%20I%20enjoy%20her%20company%20more%20than%20I%20ever%20thought%20I%20would.%20Even%20more%20surprisingly%2C%20she%20now%20seems%20to%20enjoy%20mine.%20Her%20transformation%20reminds%20me%20that%20despite%20their%20prickly%20exterior%2C%20teens%20still%20love%20(and%20need)%20their%20parents.%20%3Cbr%3E%3Cbr%3EMy%2014-year-old%20boys%20may%20still%20need%20to%20develop%20the%20skills%20required%20to%20pick%20up%20dirty%20clothes%20from%20their%20bedroom%20floor%2C%20but%20if%20I'm%20having%20a%20tough%20time%2C%20they'll%20be%20the%20first%20to%20bring%20me%20a%20drink%20of%20water%20or%20check%20that%20I'm%20OK.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAnd%20while%20I%20may%20not%20appreciate%20notes%20from%20teachers%20about%20late%20homework%2C%20these%20are%20offset%20by%20the%20pride%20I%20feel%20when%20I%20notice%20glimpses%20of%20the%20adults%20my%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2F10-teens-to-rule-the-2020s-decade-2019-12%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Echildren%20are%20becoming%3C%2Fa%3E%3A%20the%20sudden%20shifts%20toward%20a%20more%20diligent%20way%20of%20living%3B%20the%20chats%20about%20the%20future%20they're%20starting%20to%20imagine%20for%20themselves.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20relief%20and%20joy%20that%20comes%20from%20feeling%2C%20just%20for%20a%20second%2C%20that%20you%20might%20have%20got%20this%20parenting%20thing%20right%20is%20immeasurable%2C%20if%20fleeting.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22042e3d70-403a-4ef0-ab5a-bcfadd0c5eba%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EThey%20still%20drive%20me%20crazy%20at%20times%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EYes%2C%20I%20have%20to%20request%20that%20music%20be%20turned%20down%20late%20at%20night.%20I%20despair%20over%20the%20state%20of%20the%20kitchen%20after%20one%20of%20them%20has%20made%20a%20sandwich.%20It's%20hard%20when%20you%20pass%20them%20with%20their%20mates%20in%20the%20street%2C%20and%20they%20pretend%20not%20to%20see%20you.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20all%20in%20all%2C%20parenting%20teens%20is%20very%20different%20from%20what%20I'd%20imagined.%20Teens%20in%20general%20may%20not%20seem%20lovable%2C%20but%20teenage%20versions%20of%20your%20own%20children%20are%20surprisingly%20sweet%3A%20you%20recognize%20their%20angst%20is%20their%20way%20of%20protecting%20their%20vulnerability%2C%20meaning%20when%20they%20act%20up%2C%20you%20experience%20sympathy%20and%20love%20alongside%20the%20annoyance.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22d0c57d19-1a73-4410-be34-58d553774611%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3ESeeing%20who%20they%20are%20becoming%20is%20a%20huge%20reward%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EAs%20they%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwhen-does-adulthood-begin-adulting-2019-1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eprogress%20toward%20adulthood%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20I've%20noticed%20that%20my%20teens%20have%20even%20started%20to%20see%20their%20parents%20as%20people%2C%20for%20better%20or%20worse.%20They%20appreciate%20what%20you%20do%20for%20them%20a%20little%20more%2C%20even%20if%20they%20do%20sometimes%20point%20out%20your%20failings%20a%20little%20too%20accurately.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EPlus%2C%20they're%20hilarious.%20One%20of%20my%20older%20kids%20does%20brilliant%20impressions%20of%20family%20members%2C%20including%20his%20father%20(when%20he's%20not%20in%20the%20room).%20Their%20antics%20can%20have%20you%20in%20fits%20of%20giggles.%20On%20a%20good%20day%2C%20they%20have%20an%20enthusiasm%20and%20lust%20for%20life%20that%20feels%20infectious.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20not%20saying%20raising%20teens%20isn't%20a%20challenge%2C%20and%20I%20certainly%20don't%20think%20it's%20for%20the%20faint-hearted.%20But%20if%20we're%20going%20to%20point%20out%20the%20drawbacks%2C%20we%20ought%20to%20spare%20a%20little%20room%20for%20the%20things%20that%20make%20it%20absolutely%20amazing%20%E2%80%94%20and%20there%20are%20plenty%20of%20them.%3Cbr%3E%3Cbr%3E%3Cstrong%3E%3Cem%3EDo%20you%20have%20a%20hot%20take%20on%20a%20common%20parenting%20belief%3F%20Email%20Jennifer%20Beck%20Goldblatt%20at%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22mailto%3Ajgoldblatt%40insider.com%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3E%3Cem%3Ejgoldblatt%40insider.com%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cstrong%3E%3Cem%3E%20to%20share%20your%20experience%20with%20Business%20Insider.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fenjoying-parenting-raising-tweens-teens-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786193521000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a75ecad0c6c5a263f3a77f0%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fenjoying-parenting-raising-tweens-teens-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22Everyone%20warned%20me%20about%20parenting%20during%20the%20teen%20years.%20Sure%2C%20there%20are%20hard%20parts%2C%20but%20there's%20a%20fun%20side%20to%20it%2C%20too.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22insider%40insider.com%20(Gillian%20Harvey)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22The%20US%20Army%20wants%20soldiers%20to%20test%20tomorrow's%20tech%20while%20preparing%20to%20fight%20today.%20It's%20a%20balancing%20act.%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%225119%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Four%20US%20Army%20soldiers%20walk%20down%20a%20rocky%20hill%20with%20smoke%20surrounding%20them.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7455db0c6c5a263f3a6e4b%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%223414%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EThis%20year's%20Project%20Convergence%20Capstone%20combined%20combat%20realism%20and%20experimentation%20with%20new%20systems%20like%20drones.%3Cp%3EUS%20Army%20photo%20by%20Sgt.%20Nathan%20Arellano%20Tlaczani%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EThe%20US%20Army%20recently%20combined%20a%20major%20technology%20experiment%20with%20realistic%20training.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EIntegrating%20new%20weapons%20into%20training%20situations%20delivers%20both%20benefits%20and%20trade-offs.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3ESome%20soldiers%20avoided%20risk%20with%20unfamiliar%20systems%20to%20maximize%20their%20training%20time.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20US%20Army%20is%20embracing%20a%20wave%20of%20new%20weapons%20and%20systems%2C%20from%20drones%20to%20command-and-control%20platforms%2C%20and%20putting%20these%20experimental%3Cstrong%3E%20%3C%2Fstrong%3Ecapabilities%20directly%20in%20the%20hands%20of%20soldiers%20during%20training%20events.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThat%20approach%20yields%3Cstrong%3E%20%3C%2Fstrong%3Evaluable%20lessons%20and%20gives%20soldiers%20hands-on%20experience%20with%20new%20technologies.%20The%20push%20and%20pull%20of%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmarines-are-preparing-for-future-fights-but-stretched-thin-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eexperimentation%20and%20training%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20however%2C%20can%20create%20tension%20between%20testing%20unfamiliar%20gear%20and%20preparing%20units%20for%20the%20broader%20demands%20of%20warfare.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAt%20Fort%20Irwin%20in%20California%2C%20the%20Army%20recently%20conducted%20its%20Project%20Convergence%20Capstone%20exercise%2C%20a%20large-scale%20experiment%20built%20into%20a%20training%20event%20in%20the%20brutal%20heat%20of%20the%20Mojave%20Desert.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ERoughly%2010%2C000%20troops%20participated%20in%20this%20large%20multinational%20exercise%20and%20took%20part%20in%20simulated%20warfighting%20involving%20numerous%20drones%2C%20sensors%2C%20electronic%20warfare%20capabilities%2C%20and%20other%20new%20technologies%2C%20including%20the%20Army's%20prototype%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fus-army-rapidly-built-digital-command-and-control-testing-experimenting-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ecommand-and-control%20system%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Participants%20tested%20around%20100%20new%20weapons%20and%20technologies.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThis%20year%20marked%20an%20evolution%20from%20previous%20Project%20Convergence%20Capstone%20exercises%2C%20which%20mainly%20focused%20on%20soldiers%20testing%20new%20systems%20in%20dedicated%20experimentation%20lanes.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EPast%20iterations%20were%20%26quot%3Bmore%20laboratory-like%2C%20where%20we%20just%20kind%20of%20set%20that%20technology%20in%20motion%2C%20we%20do%20a%20quick%20assessment%2C%20determine%20what%20we%20want%20to%20do%20differently%2C%20and%20then%20we'll%20do%20it%20again%2C%26quot%3B%20Brig.%20Gen.%20Daniel%20Hibner%2C%20head%20of%20the%20Army%20Joint%20Modernization%20Command%2C%20said%20at%20the%20exercise%20last%20month.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20shift%20toward%20a%20more%20realistic%20combat%20scenario%20was%20driven%20in%20part%20by%20the%20Army's%20desire%20to%20stress-test%20its%20new%20command-and-control%20system%2C%20but%20the%20environment%20and%20structure%20also%20created%20conditions%20for%20evaluating%20other%20emerging%20technologies.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%228192%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22A%20US%20Army%20soldier%20puts%20together%20a%20small%20quadcopter%20drone%20that's%20sitting%20in%20a%20case%20on%20the%20ground.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7456860c6c5a263f3a6e4e%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%225464%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EOperators%20said%20they%20weren't%20pushing%20their%20drones%20so%20they%20could%20get%20more%20training%20out%20of%20the%20systems.%3Cp%3EUS%20Army%20photo%20by%20Sgt.%20Nathan%20Arellano%20Tlaczani%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20Army%20deployed%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fus-war-with-iran-shows-unseen-battle-vital-modern-war-2026-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eemitters%2C%20jammers%2C%20and%20sensors%3C%2Fa%3E%20to%20effectively%20create%20a%20denied%2C%20degraded%2C%20intermittent%2C%20and%20limited%20communications%20environment.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20Army%20said%20that%20testing%20new%20systems%20in%20a%20combat%20scenario%20against%20a%20simulated%20near-peer%20adversary%20produced%20more%20realistic%20operating%20conditions%20and%20potentially%20more%20useful%20feedback.%20That%20feedback%20could%20inform%20decisions%20ranging%20from%20whether%20the%20Army%20should%20acquire%20a%20certain%20drone%20to%20broader%20operational%20concepts%20for%20when%20and%20how%20to%20use%20specific%20weapons%20or%20tactics.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESoldiers%20said%20they%20learned%20firsthand%20how%20to%20support%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fus-army-soldiers-training-brains-fly-drones-different-to-aircraft-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Enew%20systems%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20keep%20them%20functioning%2C%20gathering%20data%20on%20questions%20such%20as%20how%20many%20drone%20batteries%20to%20bring%20to%20an%20observation%20post%20or%20how%20to%20keep%20systems%20from%20overheating.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20Army%20has%20prioritized%20this%20hands-on%20testing%20in%20recent%20years%2C%20aiming%20to%20involve%20soldiers%20early%20in%20the%20development%20of%20a%20new%20technology%20and%20use%20their%20feedback%20to%20inform%20acquisition%20decisions%20or%20help%20vendors%20refine%20their%20products.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EBut%20combining%20experimentation%20with%20training%20creates%20challenges.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ETesting%20new%20technologies%20involves%20learning%20by%20doing%3A%20evaluating%20how%20a%20system%20performs%2C%20determining%20where%20it%20might%20be%20useful%2C%20and%20developing%20tactics%20for%20employing%20it.%20The%20objectives%20are%20not%20always%20as%20clear%2C%20and%2C%20especially%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fus-soldiers-need-lots-cheap-drones-use-ammo-army-commander-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ewith%20drones%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20soldiers%20are%20still%20determining%20whether%20operating%20them%20is%20an%20additional%20task%20or%20an%20entirely%20new%20job.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAt%20Fort%20Irwin%2C%20soldiers%20were%20navigating%20these%20competing%20demands.%20Some%20told%20Business%20Insider%20they%20did%20not%20push%20their%20systems%20to%20their%20limits%20in%20the%20harsh%20conditions%20because%20they%20wanted%20more%20time%20to%20practice%20with%20the%20technology%20rather%20than%20risk%20losing%20or%20breaking%20it.%20Other%20soldiers%20said%20they%20maintained%20physical%20backups%20in%20case%20they%20lost%20access%20to%20prototype%20digital%20maps%20or%20communications.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%226645%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22One%20US%20Army%20soldier%20stands%20holding%20a%20white%20box%20while%20another%20soldier%20crouches%20holding%20a%20drone%20controller.%20The%20soldiers%20are%20in%20the%20desert.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7458a70c6c5a263f3a6e57%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%224432%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3ESoldiers%20provided%20feedback%20on%20weapons%2C%20including%20drones%20and%20the%20Army's%20new%20command%20and%20control%20system.%3Cp%3EUS%20Army%20photo%20by%20Sgt.%20Sar%20Paw%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cp%3ECertain%20aspects%20of%20the%20exercise%2C%20including%20the%20need%20to%20manage%20and%20deconflict%20airspace%20shared%20by%20soldiers%20operating%20different%20drones%2C%20also%20constrained%20how%20the%20systems%20were%20tested.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20one%20example%2C%20a%20sergeant%20operating%20an%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fanduril-president-defense-tech-companies-create-monopoly-2026-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EAnduril%20Bolt-M%20drone%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20said%20he%20hadn't%20flown%20the%20aircraft%20to%20its%20full%20range%20or%20altitude.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BWe%20could%20just%20do%20it%20safer%2C%20and%20that%20way%20we%20could%20get%20more%20repetitions%20in.%26quot%3B%20Soldiers%20can%20also%20manage%20the%20shared%20airspace.%20%26quot%3BWe're%20not%20the%20only%20people%20flying%20out%20here%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EUS%20forces%20were%20not%20the%20only%20ones%20balancing%20experimentation%20with%20training.%20British%20soldiers%20described%20two%20distinct%20processes%20for%20evaluating%20and%20integrating%20new%20drones%3A%20trials%20and%20experimentation.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ETrials%20involve%20%26quot%3Btaking%20one%20of%20these%20things%2C%26quot%3B%20Lt.%20Col.%20John%20Black%2C%20a%20British%20Army%20commander%2C%20told%20Business%20Insider%2C%20referring%20to%20drones%2C%20%26quot%3Bput%20it%20through%20its%20paces%2C%20and%20test%20it%20to%20see%20if%20it%20does%20what%20the%20Army%20wants%20it%20to%20do%26quot%3B%20before%20it's%20acquired.%20This%20includes%20safety%20and%20integration%20tests.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EExperiments%20are%20more%20focused%20on%20applying%20the%20system%20to%20specific%20use%20cases.%20For%20an%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fukraine-uncrewed-ground-vehicle-drone-usage-double-kill-zone-expand-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Euncrewed%20ground%20vehicle%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20that%20could%20mean%20examining%20whether%20it%20makes%20front-line%20logistics%20easier%20or%20safer.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20challenges%20of%20tomorrow's%20battlefields%2C%20including%20uncrewed%20systems%2C%20electronic%20warfare%2C%20and%20artificial%20intelligence%2C%20mean%20troops%20must%20acquire%20new%20skills%20while%20continuing%20to%20refine%20their%20foundational%3Cstrong%3E%20%3C%2Fstrong%3Ecombat%20skills.%20That%20demands%20a%20more%20flexible%20and%20adaptable%20mindset.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EHibner%20told%20Business%20Insider%20the%20exercise's%20goals%20were%20to%20achieve%20combat%20realism%2C%20avoid%20interfering%20with%20how%20rotational%20units%20fight%2C%20and%20introduce%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fus-army-assessing-new-ai-enabled-battlefield-tech-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Enew%20technology%3C%2Fa%3E%20that%20disrupts%20but%20doesn't%20detract%20from%20foundational%20training.%20%26quot%3BSo%20you%20bring%20in%20the%20right%20amount%20of%20tech%2C%20you%20train%20it%20in%20the%20right%20amount%2C%20put%20it%20in%20the%20hands%20of%20soldiers%20and%20leaders%2C%20and%20then%20you%20let%20them%20go%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Ftesting-new-tech-while-training-work-in-progress-us-army-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786192861000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a745a288fcc2e955f7ddb55%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Ftesting-new-tech-while-training-work-in-progress-us-army-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22Soldiers%20can%20provide%20feedback%20on%20new%20systems%2C%20but%20they%20also%20have%20to%20learn%20how%20to%20use%20them%20without%20sacrificing%20the%20combat%20training%20they%20need.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22cpanella%40businessinsider.com%20(Chris%20Panella)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22%E2%80%98Kettic%C3%A8%E2%80%99%20Review%3A%20An%20Amusing%2C%20Original%20Portrait%20of%20Adolescent%20Ennui%20Against%20a%20Backdrop%20of%20Adult%20Cluelessness%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786192200000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fvariety.com%2F%3Fp%3D1236830542%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22Monica%20Bellucci%E2%80%99s%20sneer%20is%20a%20thing%20of%20wonder%2C%20so%20why%20have%20so%20few%20directors%20used%20it%20properly%3F%20When%20allowed%20full%20rein%20to%20her%20sense%20of%20irony%2C%20as%20given%20her%20by%20Giovanni%20Tortorici%20in%20%E2%80%9CKettic%C3%A8%2C%E2%80%9D%20Bellucci%20has%20few%20equals%20in%20her%20ab