%22%3A%22My%20grandmother%20is%20dividing%20her%20assets%20while%20she's%20still%20alive.%20She%20hopes%20it%20will%20help%20our%20family%20avoid%20divisiveness%20later.%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%221590%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22The%20author%20with%20her%20grandmother%20and%20mother.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7361df3f00ff875d13d6a5%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%221193%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EThe%20author%20with%20her%20grandmother%20and%20mother.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20Lindsay%20Karp%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EBefore%20her%2090th%20birthday%2C%20my%20grandmother%20invited%20us%20over%20to%20her%20apartment.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EShe%20asked%20us%20to%20tell%20her%20which%20of%20her%20belongings%20she%20wanted.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EI%20had%20mixed%20feelings%20at%20first%20and%20told%20her%20I%20didn't%20want%20the%20paintings%20I'd%20chosen%20for%20a%20long%20time.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EWe've%20all%20heard%20stories%20of%20familial%20feud%20after%20a%20loved%20one%20passes%20and%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsplit-5-million-assets-equally-children-stepchildren-2025-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eassets%20are%20divided%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Verbal%20promises%20become%20null%20and%20void%20once%20the%20person%20who%20made%20the%20pledge%20is%20gone%20%E2%80%94%20or%20perhaps%20those%20promises%20were%20never%20made%20to%20begin%20with.%20And%20even%20words%20written%20into%20legal%20wills%20can%20spark%20arguments%20and%20resentment%20for%20years%20to%20come.%20To%20avoid%20family%20upheaval%20after%20her%20future%20passing%2C%20my%20now-95-year-old%20grandmother%20took%20matters%20into%20her%20own%20hands.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAbout%2013%20years%20ago%2C%20my%20grandparents%20moved%20into%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Famerica-elderly-housing-crisis-a-solution-backyard-norcs-retirement-2025-11%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eretirement%20community%3C%2Fa%3E.%20As%20they%20packed%20up%20their%20home%2C%20they%20sorted%20through%20belongings%2C%20selling%20furniture%20and%20giving%20away%20items%20they%20no%20longer%20had%20space%20for.%20My%20brother%20took%20a%20large%2C%20green%20antique%20lamp%2C%20and%20my%20husband%20and%20I%20took%20an%20ottoman%20that%20converted%20into%20a%20small%20bed.%20They%20were%20tiny%20reminders%20of%20a%20home%20my%20brother%20and%20I%20grew%20up%20in%20alongside%20our%20own.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22bc92cdf4-547c-4383-9f55-8b7b2e8485cb%5C%22%3EAfter%20my%20grandfather%20died%2C%20my%20grandmother%20made%20a%20request%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EA%20few%20years%20later%2C%20my%20grandfather%20passed%20away%20after%20a%20drawn-out%20battle%20with%20Alzheimer's.%20Then%2C%20before%20her%2090th%20birthday%2C%20my%20grandmother%20invited%20our%20family%20over%20in%20an%20attempt%20to%20prevent%20future%20confusion%20or%20fighting%20over%20her%20possessions.%20My%20kids%2C%20parents%2C%20brother%2C%20aunt%2C%20uncle%2C%20and%20cousins%20poured%20into%20her%20two-bedroom%20apartment%20to%20fulfill%20her%20wishes.%20%26quot%3BTell%20me%20what%20you%20want%2C%26quot%3B%20she%20said.%20%26quot%3BI'll%20put%20a%20sticky%20note%20on%20the%20back%20with%20your%20name%20on%20it.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20was%20hesitant%20to%20respond.%20My%20grandmother%20was%20my%20second%20mother%2C%20always%20stepping%20in%20during%20my%20childhood%20when%20needed.%20When%20my%20mom%20caught%20chickenpox%20from%20me%20at%2033%20and%20was%20laid%20up%20in%20bed%2C%20my%20grandmother%20came%20over%20to%20apply%20my%20makeup%20before%20a%20dance%20recital.%20She%20cared%20for%20my%20brother%20and%20me%20for%20a%20week%20while%20my%20parents%20were%20away%20when%20I%20was%20in%206th%20grade%2C%20and%20she%20was%20present%20at%20every%20orchestra%20concert%20and%20commencement%20ceremony.%20A%20ceramic%20bowl%20or%20sectional%20sofa%20could%20never%20replace%20her.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EPutting%20my%20name%20on%20the%20back%20of%20a%20vase%20couldn't%20ease%20the%20idea%20that%20my%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandmother-aging-perspective-positive-outlook-longevity-2026-1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Egrandmother%20was%20getting%20older%3C%2Fa%3E.%20And%20it%20certainly%20can't%20replace%20grief%20with%20happiness%20when%20she's%20gone.%20But%20it%20was%20what%20she%20wanted.%20%26quot%3BIt%20will%20make%20me%20happy%20to%20know%20this%20work%20is%20done%2C%26quot%3B%20she%20said.%20%26quot%3BI%20don't%20want%20any%20fighting%20when%20I'm%20gone.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%223c4fd8ed-e793-4670-96d5-74b9c210f871%5C%22%3EI%20chose%20a%20few%20belongings%2C%20though%20I%20had%20mixed%20feelings%20about%20it%20at%20first%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20her%20younger%20years%2C%20my%20grandmother%20was%20a%20watercolorist.%20Her%20walls%20are%20covered%20with%20her%20personal%20artwork%2C%20capturing%20strokes%20of%20her%20paintbrush%20from%20long%20ago.%20%26quot%3BI'd%20love%20this%20one%2C%26quot%3B%20my%20mom%20said%2C%20pointing%20to%20a%20rustic%20painting%20of%20a%20barn.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIf%20I%20didn't%20speak%20up%2C%20I%20wouldn't%20have%20a%20piece%20of%20my%20grandmother%20on%20the%20walls%20of%20my%20house%20when%20I%20need%20it%20most.%20There%20is%20no%20better%20way%20to%20feel%20someone's%20presence%20than%20through%20something%20they%20created%20themselves.%20%26quot%3BI%20want%20this%20one%2C%26quot%3B%20I%20said%2C%20pointing%20to%20the%20painting%20of%20a%20young%20girl%2C%20one%20my%20grandmother%20and%20I%20always%20joked%20was%20me.%20That%20day%2C%20my%20name%20was%20written%20on%20a%20sticky%20note%20stuck%20to%20the%20backs%20of%20two%20of%20her%20paintings%20and%20on%20various%20other%20belongings.%20It%20left%20me%20with%20a%20feeling%20of%20discomfort%2C%20but%20I%20told%20her%2C%20%26quot%3BI%20don't%20want%20them%20for%20a%20very%20long%20time.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EFor%20the%20next%20couple%20of%20hours%20%E2%80%94%20and%20even%20over%20the%20next%20few%20years%20%E2%80%94%20sticky%20notes%20with%20our%20names%20were%20added%20onto%20the%20back%20of%20every%20painting%20and%20the%20bottom%20of%20every%20belonging%20in%20her%20apartment.%20Even%20my%2014-%20and%2011-year-old%20boys%20have%20chosen%20an%20item%20from%20her%20home.%20When%20a%20sprinkling%20of%20sticky%20notes%20appeared%20throughout%20her%20floors%2C%20she%20moved%20our%20names%20and%20items%20onto%20a%20list%20on%20paper.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22fcd5df04-ba8c-4b9f-a8d5-71c26eb4cf64%5C%22%3EI'm%20glad%20my%20grandmother%20started%20the%20conversation%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EI'm%20unsure%20where%20the%20paper%20is%20or%20if%20we'll%20be%20able%20to%20find%20it%20when%20the%20time%20comes.%20But%20my%20grandmother%20made%20sure%20we%20took%20time%20to%20choose%20the%20pieces%20of%20her%20that%20we'd%20like%20to%20remember%20her%20by.%20She%20gave%20herself%20peace%20of%20mind%20by%20starting%20a%20conversation%20most%20never%20have%2C%20and%20I'm%20so%20glad%20she%20did.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EOne%20day%2C%20when%20I%20can't%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2F101-year-old-grandma-many-friends-secrets-building-community-social-2026-1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Evisit%20with%20my%20grandmother%3C%2Fa%3E%20or%20hear%20her%20voice%20on%20the%20other%20end%20of%20the%20line%2C%20I'll%20have%20her%20paintings%20on%20the%20walls%20of%20my%20home.%20Bits%20and%20pieces%20of%20her%20will%20be%20sprinkled%20throughout%20my%20house%2C%20and%20if%20I'm%20lucky%2C%20there%20just%20may%20be%20a%20sticky%20note%20hiding%20on%20the%20back%20with%20my%20name%20on%20it.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandmother-dividing-her-assets-now-help-family-avoid-fighting-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786184461000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7361df3f00ff875d13d6a5%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandmother-dividing-her-assets-now-help-family-avoid-fighting-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22My%20grandmother%20is%20dividing%20her%20assets%20while%20she's%20still%20alive.%20I%20had%20mixed%20feelings%20about%20it%20at%20first%2C%20but%20I'm%20glad%20she%20started%20the%20conversation.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22insider%40insider.com%20(Lindsay%20Karp)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22He%20joined%20OpenAI.%20Here%E2%80%99s%20his%20advice%20for%20those%20who%20want%20a%20job%20at%20the%20lab.%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%222000%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22OpenAI%20product%20manager%20Ty%20Geri%20is%20pictured.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a6bb21ea62e6e00bc538aab%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%221500%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3ETy%20Geri%20is%20a%20product%20manager%20at%20OpenAI.%20He%20said%20the%20lab%20hires%20passionate%20people%20who%20experiment%20with%20the%20product.%3Cp%3ETy%20Geri%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EOpenAI%20product%20manager%20Ty%20Geri%20told%20Business%20Insider%20his%20advice%20for%20landing%20land%20a%20job%20at%20the%20AI%20lab.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EGeri%20said%20to%20be%20passionate%20about%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-updated-principles-three-key-changes-competition-agi-anthropic-2026-4%5C%22%20data-autoaffiliated%3D%5C%22false%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3EOpenAI's%20mission%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20and%20to%20consistently%20experiment%20with%20the%20tools.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EHe%20shared%20one%20of%20OpenAI's%20most%20distinctive%20(and%20sometimes%20stressful)%20expectations%3A%20%26quot%3Bbuilding%20in%20public.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3EOpenAI%20job%20seekers%2C%20listen%20up.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ETy%20Geri%20joined%20the%20AI%20lab%20in%202025%20as%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fsalary-journeys-40k-to-250k-product-manager-business-school-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eproduct%20manager%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Business%20Insider%20asked%20for%20his%20advice%20on%20landing%20a%20job%20at%20OpenAI%20%E2%80%94%C2%A0and%20he%20said%20that%20enthusiasm%20was%20key.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BI%20think%20OpenAI%20tries%20to%20hire%20people%20who%20are%20really%20passionate%2C%20and%20care%2C%20and%20want%20to%20be%20a%20part%20of%20this%20mission%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EGeri's%20advice%20is%20agnostic%20of%20role%2C%20he%20said%3A%20engineer%2C%20researcher%2C%20product%20manager%2C%20data%20scientist%2C%20whatever.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EHis%20other%20advice%20was%20to%20use%20the%20company's%20products.%20That%20doesn't%20mean%20he%20expects%20all%20the%20products%20to%20work%20instantaneously.%20Some%20will%20be%20%26quot%3Ba%20little%20rough%20today%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said%2C%20but%20OpenAI%20is%20looking%20for%20people%20who%20are%20willing%20to%20%26quot%3Bpush%20on%20the%20frontiers.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BTry%20to%20bring%20these%20products%20into%20your%20life%2C%20into%20your%20workflows%2C%26quot%3B%20Geri%20advised.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20July%2C%20a%20former%20OpenAI%20intern%20shared%20his%20advice%20with%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-intern-tips-breaking-into-ai-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E.%20He%20said%3A%20go%20broad%2C%20specialize%2C%20and%20build.%20Another%20OpenAI%20employee%20said%20he%20got%20his%20job%20thanks%20in%20part%20to%20a%20cold%20DM%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fcold-linkedin-message-landed-me-my-job-at-openai-2025-7%3Futm_source%3Dchatgpt.com%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eon%20LinkedIn%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ESundeep%20Teki%2C%20a%20career%20coach%20who%20helps%20place%20talent%20at%20AI%20companies%2C%20told%20Business%20Insider%20in%20June%20that%20OpenAI%20had%20one%20of%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fwhy-everybody-wants-to-work-at-anthropic-or-openai-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ehardest%20technical%20interviews%3C%2Fa%3E%20in%20the%20industry.%20So%2C%20study%20up.%20Also%2C%20the%20labs%20sometimes%20recruit%20people%20from%20their%20public%20profiles%2C%20so%20keep%20contributing%20to%20that%20GitHub.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAs%20for%20Geri%2C%20he%20said%20that%20the%20messiness%20of%20experimentation%20was%20core%20to%20OpenAI's%20culture.%20The%20company%20expects%20%26quot%3Ba%20lot%20of%20building%20in%20public%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EStaffers%20at%20the%20company%20want%20to%20see%20what%20you're%20building%20and%20try%20it%20out%20for%20themselves%2C%20Geri%20said.%20He%20described%20a%20fallacy%20of%20work%3A%20%26quot%3BYou%20sit%20in%20a%20dark%20room%2C%20you%20come%20out%20three%20years%20later%2C%20and%20you're%20like%3A%20'Voila%2C%20magic.'%26quot%3B%20That%20doesn't%20fly%20at%20OpenAI.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BIt%20definitely%20stresses%20me%20out%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said%2C%20%26quot%3Bbut%20I%20think%20it's%20part%20of%20the%20fun.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAmong%20OpenAI%20employees%2C%20Geri%20said%20that%20there%20was%20a%20willingness%20to%20try%20new%20things.%20If%20the%20product%20you%20put%20out%20is%20%26quot%3Bnot%20quite%20it%20yet%2C%26quot%3B%20Geri%20said%20that%20others%20at%20the%20company%20will%20try%20again.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20culture%20of%20experimentation%20and%20%26quot%3Bbig%20swings%2C%26quot%3B%20as%20Geri%20calls%20them%2C%20is%20also%20what%20makes%20OpenAI%20different%20from%20his%20prior%20job%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fjeff-dean-leaves-google-employees-react-fond-memes-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eat%20Google%3C%2Fa%3E.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BLarger%20companies%20in%20the%20space%20can%20sometimes%20be%20a%20little%20bit%20slower%2C%26quot%3B%20he%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-hiring-job-advice-from-product-manager-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786183381000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a6bb21ea62e6e00bc538aab%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fopenai-hiring-job-advice-from-product-manager-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22OpenAI%20product%20manager%20Ty%20Geri%20told%20Business%20Insider%20that%20the%20AI%20lab%20hires%20people%20who%20are%20passionate%20about%20the%20mission%20and%20experiment.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22hchandonnet%40insider.com%20(Henry%20Chandonnet)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22FSSAI%20calls%20Diageo's%20'matured%20in%20American%20oak%20casks'%20claim%20misleading%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786182659000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fbsmedia.business-standard.com%2F_media%2Fbs%2Fimg%2Farticle%2F2016-10%2F17%2Fthumb%2Ffitandfill%2F1200X628%2F1476709501-2004.jpg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.business-standard.com%2Fcompanies%2Fnews%2Ffssai-calls-diageo-s-matured-in-american-oak-casks-claim-misleading-126080800720_1.html%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22United%20Spirits%20told%20stock%20exchanges%20this%20week%20it%20anticipated%20no%20financial%20implications%20from%20the%20ban%20but%20%E2%80%8Bit%20was%20closely%20monitoring%20the%20matter%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A90%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.business-standard.com%2Fcompanies%2Fnews%2Ffssai-calls-diageo-s-matured-in-american-oak-casks-claim-misleading-126080800720_1.html%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww-business--standard-com.cdn.ampproject.org%2Fc%2Fs%2Fwww.business-standard.com%2Famp%2Fcompanies%2Fnews%2Ffssai-calls-diageo-s-matured-in-american-oak-casks-claim-misleading-126080800720_1.html%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.business-standard.com%2Famp%2Fcompanies%2Fnews%2Ffssai-calls-diageo-s-matured-in-american-oak-casks-claim-misleading-126080800720_1.html%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22We%20were%20finally%20empty%20nesters.%20Then%20we%20got%20custody%20of%20our%20granddaughter%20and%20had%20to%20go%20back%20to%20work%20to%20raise%20her.%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%221320%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Connie%20and%20Michael%20Frost%20have%20been%20raising%20their%20teenage%20granddaughter%2C%20Kinsley.%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a74e8d30c6c5a263f3a7338%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%22908%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EConnie%20and%20Michael%20Frost%20have%20been%20raising%20their%20teenage%20granddaughter%2C%20Kinsley.%3Cp%3EConnie%20Frost%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3EMichael%20and%20Connie%20Frost%2C%20in%20Georgia%2C%20are%20raising%20their%2013-year-old%20granddaughter%2C%20Kinsley%2C%20full-time.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EMichael%20said%20he%20went%20back%20to%20work%20shortly%20after%20Kinsley%20came%20under%20his%20care%20to%20afford%20raising%20her.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EMichael%20and%20Connie%20have%20tried%20to%20provide%20her%20with%20a%20stable%20home%20and%20a%20strong%20education.%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3E%3Cem%3EThis%20as-told-to%20essay%20is%20based%20on%20a%20conversation%20with%20Michael%20Frost%2C%2067%2C%20and%20his%20wife%20Connie%2C%2063%2C%20who%20are%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandparents-raising-grandchildren-sacrificing-retirement-health-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cem%3Eraising%20their%20teenage%20granddaughter%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cem%3E%20in%20Georgia.%20They%20have%20permanent%20custody%20of%20her%20and%20said%20they've%20prioritized%20providing%20her%20with%20a%20%3C%2Fem%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flived-in-toolshed-recession-help-build-business-2025-12%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cem%3Estable%20home%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cem%3E%20and%20strong%20education.%20This%20interview%20has%20been%20edited%20for%20length%20and%20clarity.%3C%2Fem%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMICHAEL%3A%20My%20wife%20and%20I%20have%20been%20raising%20Kinsley%2C%20our%20granddaughter%2C%20since%20she%20was%202%20years%20old.%20Now%2C%20she's%2013.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThis%20is%20the%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Festate-tax-qtip-trust-second-marriage-inheritance-wealth-2023-12%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Esecond%20marriage%3C%2Fa%3E%20for%20both%20my%20wife%20and%20me%2C%20and%20we%20married%20in%202012.%20I%20have%20three%20daughters%2C%20and%20she%20has%20four.%20I%20tease%20everybody%20that%20we%20live%20on%20the%20%26quot%3BEstrogen%20Ranch.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20family%20owns%20a%20party%20rental%20business%2C%20where%20you%20can%20rent%20anything%20from%20a%20large%20excavator%20to%20a%20lawnmower%20to%20tents%20and%20chairs.%20Two%20of%20my%20daughters%20are%20also%20in%20that%20business.%20My%20wife%20has%20long%20worked%20in%20ministry%2C%20and%20she%20did%20event%20planning%20for%20church%20events%20and%20weddings.%3C%2Fp%3E%5Cn%3Caside%3E%5Cn%3Cp%3EBusiness%20Insider%20is%20looking%20to%20hear%20from%20grandparents%20who%20are%20caring%20for%20their%20grandchildren%20and%20older%20Americans%20caring%20for%20younger%20loved%20ones.%20%3Cstrong%3EShare%20your%20story%20by%20filling%20out%20this%20%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3Ca%20rel%3D%5C%22%20nofollow%5C%22%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fdocs.google.com%2Fforms%2Fd%2Fe%2F1FAIpQLSc3B3DqRcKUfGoxcUcf_oEPQOwyzJf0I-jL15r4T_XT_ZOs1Q%2Fviewform%3Fusp%3Dpreview%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3Equick%20form%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fa%3E%3Cstrong%3E.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fp%3E%5Cn%3C%2Faside%3E%5Cn%3Cp%3EI%20retired%20in%202010.%20My%20family%20had%20a%20farm%20in%20Winston%2C%20which%20is%20about%20an%20hour%20from%20Atlanta.%20My%20family%20bought%20the%20farm%20in%201987.%20My%20parents%20died%20in%202009%2C%20and%20I%20bought%20the%20farm%20from%20the%20estate%20in%202010.%20It's%2057%20acres%2C%20and%20we%20have%20cows%2C%20goats%2C%20and%20chickens%2C%20as%20well%20as%20sawmills%20and%20a%20pottery%20studio.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20have%2020%20grandchildren%20and%20one%20great-grandchild.%20It's%20a%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fvacations-large-big-family-too-expensive-how-to-save-money-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Elarge%20family%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20and%20we%20try%20to%20be%20as%20present%20as%20we%20can%20in%20their%20lives.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22348f5bc5-2640-41c3-a75c-05966438e4f8%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EWe%20were%20empty-nesters%20for%20almost%20two%20years.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EMICHAEL%3A%20After%20we%20got%20married%2C%20our%20children%20were%20all%20out%20of%20the%20house%2C%20and%20it%20was%20awesome%20being%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fempty-nesters-sold-house-live-rv-full-time-2026-1%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eempty%20nesters%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Kinsley's%20mother%20had%20moved%20around%20a%20lot.%20Kinsley%20was%20in%20some%20situations%20that%20weren't%20great.%20Her%20mother%2C%20Connie's%20daughter%2C%20was%20also%20in%20and%20out%20of%20the%20hospital%20with%20liver%20disease%20and%20wouldn't%20see%20Kinsley%20for%20a%20few%20months%20at%20a%20time.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAfter%20a%20series%20of%20liver%20transplants%2C%20she%20improved%20and%20has%20her%20own%20place.%20She%20had%20another%20child%20whom%20she%20is%20raising.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20were%20granted%20temporary%20custody%20of%20Kinsley%2C%20then%20won%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandparents-raising-grandchildren-aging-retirement-caregiving-custody-housing-financial-struggles-2026-3%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Epermanent%20custody%3C%2Fa%3E.%20I%20knew%20that%20this%20was%20going%20to%20be%20at%20least%2018%20years%20of%20taking%20care%20of%20a%20child%20again.%20I%20wouldn't%20be%20an%20empty%20nester%20again%20until%20I%20was%2072.%20I%20didn't%20want%20to%20do%20this%2C%20but%20there%20was%20nobody%20else%20willing%20to%20do%20it.%20My%20wife%20believed%20this%20would%20be%20only%20temporary.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EThis%20was%20all%20about%20safety.%20My%20wife%20has%20so%20much%20compassion%20and%20is%20willing%20to%20do%20anything.%20I'm%20not%20saying%20I'm%20not%20that%20way%2C%20but%20I%20also%20understand%20that%20people%20have%20responsibilities.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ECONNIE%3A%20The%20adjustment%20was%20hard.%20She%20couldn't%20sleep%20in%20the%20bed%20by%20herself%2C%20so%20we%20had%20to%20tag-team%20until%20she%20was%20asleep.%20We%20made%20her%20a%20really%20cool%20bed%20and%20playhouse.%20Mike%20has%20a%20great%20sense%20of%20humor%2C%20and%20he's%20been%20super%20gracious%2C%20especially%20given%20that%20he's%20not%20related%20to%20her.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMICHAEL%3A%20We%20expected%20there%20would%20be%20differences%20between%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fitalian-vs-american-parenting-differences-raising-kids-southern-italy-2026-7%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eraising%20our%20children%3C%2Fa%3E%20and%20raising%20Kinsley.%20We're%20much%20older%20now%2C%20so%20in%20all%20her%20school%20activities%2C%20it%20felt%20awkward%20that%20the%20parents%20of%20all%20the%20other%20kids%20were%20our%20children's%20age.%20But%20we%20now%20have%20a%20lot%20of%20friends%20that%20age.%20We%20also%20sent%20Kinsley%20to%20a%20private%20school%20because%20we%20didn't%20have%20confidence%20in%20where%20her%20education%20was%20headed.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%22a41a6426-b295-48f7-b1fe-d0624bf55d87%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3ERaising%20her%20has%20been%20complete%20bliss.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3ECONNIE%3A%20There%20were%20plenty%20of%20challenges%2C%20though.%20We%20have%20a%20lot%20of%20grandchildren%2C%20and%20when%20she%20was%20very%20small%2C%20she%20was%20always%20sharing%20her%20toys%20and%20room%20with%20the%20other%20grandkids%20who%20came%20over.%20It%20was%20a%20challenge%20to%20share%20attention.%20It's%20a%20tug-of-war%20in%20my%20heart%20to%20make%20sure%20that%20when%20Mike's%20grandchildren%20from%20his%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fmet-my-husband-in-my-seventies-after-retiring-from-work-2025-10%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eprevious%20marriage%3C%2Fa%3E%20are%20here%2C%20they%20have%20time%20with%20him%20without%20Kinsley.%20She%20feels%20like%20she%20owns%20the%20place.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EShe%20definitely%20runs%20us%20now.%20She's%20such%20a%20great%20kid%2C%20and%20we're%20really%20blessed.%20She%20was%20always%20very%20busy%20and%20active%2C%20but%20she's%20always%20been%20gracious%20with%20people.%20She%20can%20get%20along%20with%20just%20about%20anybody.%20We're%20trying%20to%20teach%20her%20to%20be%20generous%20and%20kind.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20wanted%20her%20to%20have%20her%20own%20space%2C%20and%20she%20needed%20to%20feel%20like%20we%20were%20the%20nucleus.%20I%20try%20to%20keep%20her%20busy%20because%20we%20don't%20want%20the%20other%20grandkids%20to%20be%20jealous%20of%20her.%20We%20eventually%20established%20that%20we're%20not%20grandparenting%20her%20but%20are%20instead%20parenting%20her.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe%20have%20some%20friends%20who%20are%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandparents-raising-grandchildren-retirement-foster-care-aging-insurance-financial-instability-2026-5%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eraising%20grandkids%3C%2Fa%3E%2C%20but%20we%20have%20it%20a%20lot%20differently.%20We've%20had%20to%20tighten%20our%20belts%20a%20lot%2C%20especially%20recently.%20Now%20that%20we're%20not%20out%20in%20the%20world%20as%20much%2C%20we%20rely%20on%20whatever's%20been%20set%20up%20for%20retirement.%20I%20tell%20Kinsley%2C%20much%20like%20I%20told%20my%20daughters%2C%20that%20they%20have%20more%20than%20we%20ever%20had.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%2223100380-b74d-4a4d-be11-ff440d88a96f%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3EWe%20don't%20have%20as%20much%20put%20away%20as%20I%20would%20like%20to%20have%20had%20at%20this%20age%2C%20but%20we're%20OK.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EMICHAEL%3A%20We%20aren't%20solely%20relying%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Flong-term-care-cant-retire-caregiving-social-security-medicaid-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3ESocial%20Security%3C%2Fa%3E.%20We%20have%20some%20rental%20properties%20that%20help%20us.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EI%20turn%20all%20my%20hobbies%20into%20businesses%2C%20and%20we've%20tried%20to%20make%20this%20more%20of%20an%20active%20farm%20than%20just%20a%20hobby%20farm.%20There%20are%20days%20when%20I%20wonder%20if%20we%20should%20try%20to%20stop%20because%20it%20costs%20more%20than%20what%20we%20make%20from%20it%2C%20but%20we%20need%20to%20add%20to%20our%20income.%20We%20also%20jump%20in%20to%20help%20my%20daughters%20when%20they're%20overwhelmed.%20Connie%20recently%20started%20volunteering%20to%20help%20them%20out%20with%20linens.%20We%20always%20look%20for%20ways%20to%20increase%20our%20income%20and%20reduce%20expenses.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ECONNIE%3A%20We're%20not%20wealthy%2C%20though%20some%20of%20our%20grandchildren%20think%20that%20we%20are.%20Kinsley%20had%20to%20have%20surgery%20on%20her%20foot%20last%20year%2C%20and%20it%20was%20very%20expensive.%20We%20were%20looking%20at%20dental%20work%2C%20and%20all%20these%20extra%20expenses%20have%20piled%20up.%20It's%20hard%20not%20to%20think%20in%20those%20terms.%20We%20have%20to%20plan%20for%20all%20these%20things%20again%2C%20though%20we%20thought%20they%20were%20behind%20us.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Ch2%20data-toc-id%3D%5C%226591b6c9-7a99-4e36-a23a-405860b63d77%5C%22%3E%3Cstrong%3ERaising%20her%20hasn't%20been%20too%20strenuous%20on%20us.%3C%2Fstrong%3E%3C%2Fh2%3E%3Cp%3EMICHAEL%3A%20We%20are%20homeschooling%20her%20this%20year%20in%20hopes%20of%20traveling%20more%20and%20having%20her%20with%20us.%20There%20is%20a%20lot%20of%20traveling%20we%20would%20have%20liked%20to%20do%20that%20friends%20our%20age%20can%20do.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20heart%20goes%20out%20to%20people%20who%20are%20in%20their%2070s%2C%20and%20all%20of%20a%20sudden%20get%20a%202-year-old.%20We%20were%20fortunate%20to%20be%20both%20younger%20and%20active%20when%20we%20got%20Kinsley.%20It%20does%20get%20taxing%2C%20though%2C%20when%20a%20lot%20of%20our%20grandkids%20come%20and%20stay%20with%20us.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EMy%20daughters%20like%20to%20tell%20me%20that%20I%20allow%20Kinsley%20to%20do%20things%20that%20they%20were%20never%20allowed%20to%20do.%20I%20don't%20feel%20we're%20that%20far%20off%20from%20how%20we%20parented%20our%20girls%2C%20though.%20We're%20more%20strict%20than%20her%20peers'%20parents%20are.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EElectronics%20weren't%20involved%20when%20we%20raised%20our%20daughters.%20Kinsley%20just%20got%20her%20first%20iPhone%2C%20but%20for%20five%20years%2C%20all%20her%20friends%20had%20them%2C%20and%20we%20resisted.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3ECONNIE%3A%20I%20try%20to%20watch%20what%20she's%20doing%2C%20and%20maybe%20it's%20because%20we're%20older%2C%20but%20the%20electronics%20thing%20is%20a%20whole%20other%20world%2C%20and%20I%20don't%20think%20it's%20healthy.%20I%20don't%20have%20a%20problem%20knee-jerking%20this%20tech%20out%20of%20her%20hands.%20The%20kids%20are%20bombarded%20online.%20We%20don't%20care%20so%20much%20about%20what%20she%20thinks%20of%20us%20as%20much%20as%20a%20lot%20of%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fyoung-parent-empty-nester-at-40-energy-travel-hobbies-2025-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Eyoung%20parents%3C%2Fa%3E%20do%20because%20we%20know%20that%20eventually%20the%20kids%20are%20going%20to%20come%20back%20and%20say%2C%20%26quot%3BThank%20you%20for%20doing%20that.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EWe're%20pushing%20her%20to%20get%20a%20scholarship.%20We%20do%20tease%20her%20about%20taking%20care%20of%20us%20when%20we're%20old.%20We%20don't%20believe%20she%20should%20bear%20that%20burden%2C%20but%20she%20jokes%20about%20it%20and%20says%2C%20%26quot%3BYou%20could%20adopt%20me.%26quot%3B%20The%20consensus%20among%20everyone%20in%20our%20family%20is%20that%20she%20belongs%20here.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandparents-raising-grandchildren-retirement-return-to-work-social-security-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786182421000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a74eb070c6c5a263f3a734e%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fgrandparents-raising-grandchildren-retirement-return-to-work-social-security-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22Michael%20and%20Connie%20Frost%20are%20raising%20their%20granddaughter%20Kinsley%20in%20Georgia%2C%20balancing%20their%20retirement%20and%20her%20education%20needs.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22nsheidlower%40businessinsider.com%20(Noah%20Sheidlower)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22ampUrl%22%3A%22%22%7D%2C%7B%22title%22%3A%22Arena%20AI%20CEO%20says%20enterprises%20don%E2%80%99t%20know%20which%20AI%20models%20to%20trust%22%2C%22content%22%3A%22%3Cfigure%3E%3Cimg%20width%3D%5C%221440%5C%22%20alt%3D%5C%22Anastasios%20Angelopoulos%20poses%20for%20a%20photo%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7631bd0c6c5a263f3a7b75%3Fformat%3Djpeg%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%221080%5C%22%3E%3Cfigcaption%3EArena%20CEO%20Anastasios%20Angelopoulos%20said%20companies%20have%20told%20him%20they%20are%20struggling%20to%20decide%20which%20AI%20models%20to%20trust.%3Cp%3ECourtesy%20of%20Arena%20AI%3C%2Fp%3E%3C%2Ffigcaption%3E%3C%2Ffigure%3E%3Cul%3E%3Cli%3ECompanies%20are%20struggling%20to%20decide%20which%20AI%20models%20to%20use%2C%20Arena%20CEO%20Anastasios%20Angelopoulos%20said.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EAngelopoulos%20said%20enterprises%20have%20reasons%20to%20be%20skeptical%20of%20frontier%20labs%20and%20Chinese%20open%20models.%3C%2Fli%3E%3Cli%3EAngelopoulos%20told%20Business%20Insider%20that%20it's%20%26quot%3Ba%20really%20tricky%20situation.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fli%3E%3C%2Ful%3E%3Cp%3ECompanies%20don't%20know%20which%20side%20to%20choose%20in%20AI%2C%20the%20leader%20of%20one%20of%20the%20largest%20model%20evaluators%20said.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BIt's%20not%20only%20true%20that%20they're%20terrified%20of%20working%20with%20the%20frontier%20labs%2C%20but%20they're%20also%20terrified%20of%20working%20with%20the%20Chinese%20open%20source%2C%26quot%3B%20Arena%20CEO%20Anastasios%20Angelopoulos%20said%20during%20a%20recent%20episode%20of%20the%20%26quot%3B20VC%26quot%3B%20podcast.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAngelopoulos%20said%20the%20companies%20he%20talks%20to%20are%20struggling%20to%20figure%20out%20where%20to%20build%20their%20AI%20future.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BI%20think%20we're%20in%20a%20really%20tricky%20situation%20for%20enterprises%20because%20just%20the%20way%20that%20the%20cards%20have%20landed%2C%26quot%3B%20Angelopoulos%20told%20Business%20Insider%20during%20an%20interview%20where%20he%20expanded%20on%20his%20comments.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%20data-script%3D%5C%22%5C%22%20data-styles%3D%5C%22default-width%5C%22%20data-embed-type%3D%5C%22youtube%5C%22%20data-type%3D%5C%22embed%5C%22%3E%3Ciframe%20referrerpolicy%3D%5C%22strict-origin-when-cross-origin%5C%22%20allowfullscreen%3D%5C%22%5C%22%20src%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.youtube.com%2Fembed%2Fb_VUAev1Lmc%3Fstart%3D1808%26feature%3Doembed%5C%22%20width%3D%5C%22560%5C%22%20title%3D%5C%22Arena%20CEO%3A%20There%20Will%20be%20a%20%24100BN%20US%20Open-Source%20Model%20%26amp%3B%20Data%20is%20a%20Trillion%20Dollar%20Market%5C%22%20height%3D%5C%22315%5C%22%3E%3C%2Fiframe%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%3Cp%3EThe%20current%20situation%20is%2C%20by%20all%20accounts%2C%20a%20bit%20messy.%20Arena%20has%20an%20up-close%20view.%20The%20company%20offers%20a%20crowdsourced%20AI%20model%20battle%20royale%20that%20lets%20users%20pit%20generative%20AI%20models%20against%20each%20other%20and%20vote%20on%20which%20one%20best%20completes%20the%20task.%20In%20September%2C%20it%20announced%20a%20commercial%20business%20where%20it%20would%20sell%20AI%20companies%20and%20businesses%20data%20gathered%20from%20the%20battles.%20In%20June%2C%20Arena%20announced%20it%20had%20reached%20%24100%20million%20in%20annualized%20run-rate%20revenue%20within%208%20months%20of%20launching%20its%20enterprise%20service.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EFrontier%20AI%20companies%2C%20including%20OpenAI%20and%20Anthropic%2C%20offer%20cutting-edge%20models%2C%20but%20that%20technology%20can%20come%20with%20a%20steep%20price%20tag.%20The%20Trump%20administration's%20recent%20actions%20also%20illustrate%20that%20the%20model%20providers%20can%20be%20forced%20to%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fusing-anthropics-fable-when-foreign-access-disappeared-mid-project-2026-6%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Eshut%20off%20access%20without%20warning%3C%2Fa%3E.%20Those%20companies%2C%20as%20Anthropic%20has%20demonstrated%2C%20can%20also%20impose%20safeguards%20on%20the%20models%2C%20which%20may%20mean%20that%20many%20companies%20cannot%20access%20the%20full%20extent%20of%20the%20model's%20capabilities.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BAnthropic%20or%20OpenAI%20could%20decide%20to%20turn%20off%20their%20AI%20at%20any%20moment%20if%20they%20feel%20that%20it%20is%2C%20quote%20unquote%2C%20'unsafe%2C'%26quot%3B%20Angelopoulos%20told%20Business%20Insider.%20%26quot%3BAnd%20so%20if%20you're%20a%20business%2C%20what%20are%20you%20supposed%20to%20do%3F%20You%20want%20to%20be%20able%20to%20build%20on%20a%20stable%20and%20reliable%20AI%20stack.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EIn%20contrast%2C%20China-based%20open%20model%20companies%2C%20including%20Moonshot%20and%20DeepSeek%2C%20offer%20open-weight%20models%20that%20can%20be%20run%20locally%2C%20often%20at%20a%20fraction%20of%20the%20cost%20of%20frontier%20models.%20Some%20are%20worried%20about%20the%20security%20risks%20of%20relying%20on%20Chinese%20companies.%20Last%20month%2C%20Axios%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.axios.com%2F2026%2F07%2F20%2Fai-us-china-open-source-kimi%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22_blank%5C%22%3Ereported%3C%2Fa%3E%20that%20the%20Trump%20administration%20has%20considered%20imposing%20restrictions%20or%20even%20issuing%20de%20facto%20bans%20on%20Chinese%20models.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAngelopoulos%20isn't%20the%20only%20one%20to%20hit%20on%20these%20themes.%20P%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fpalantir-alex-karp-ai-labs-colonize-enterprise-q2-earnings-call-2026-8%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3Ealantir%20CEO%20Alex%20Karp%20has%20repeatedly%20warned%3C%2Fa%3E%20that%20frontier%20AI%20companies%2C%20with%20which%20Palantir%20works%2C%20want%20to%20gather%20valuable%20intellectual%20property%20and%20data%20that%20they%20could%20then%20use%20to%20compete%20with%20their%20current%20customers.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BThey%20deserve%20to%20colonize%20your%20enterprise%2C%26quot%3B%20Karp%20said%20during%20Palantir's%20second-quarter%20earnings%20call%20on%20Monday%2C%20characterizing%20what%20he%20believed%20was%20the%20labs'%20attitude.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EPalantir%20and%20Karp%20also%20have%20some%20incentive%20to%20stoke%20those%20fears%2C%20as%20the%20company%20offers%20its%20customers%20an%20application%20layer%20that%20allows%20businesses%20to%20control%20their%20data%20and%20the%20AI%20models%20they%20use.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3EAngelopoulos%20said%20Arena%20has%20experienced%20its%20own%20struggles%20with%20AI%20companies.%20He%20said%20that%20Arena%20has%20seen%20model%20providers%20use%20Arena's%20internal%20data%20%26quot%3Bto%20serve%20synthetic%20battles%20and%20arenas%20to%20our%20employees%20in%20an%20effort%20to%20essentially%20get%20them%20to%20label%20data.%26quot%3B%20Angelopoulos%20declined%20to%20name%20the%20offending%20companies%2C%20but%20said%20the%20practice%20%26quot%3Bis%20not%20uncommon.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Fjensen-huang%5C%22%20target%3D%5C%22%5C%22%3ENvidia%20CEO%20Jensen%20Huang%2C%3C%2Fa%3E%20whose%20company%20does%20business%20with%20frontier%20model%20makers%20and%20offers%20open%20models%2C%20has%20tried%20to%20strike%20a%20balance%20in%20the%20debate.%20He%20has%20said%20that%20companies%20will%20deploy%20both%20open%20models%20and%20proprietary%20ones%2C%20routing%20tasks%20based%20on%20both%20cost%20effectiveness%20and%20maintaining%20their%20IP.%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cp%3E%26quot%3BThe%20world%20is%20going%20to%20have%20closed%20and%20open%20models%2C%26quot%3B%20Huang%20recently%20told%20Axios.%20%26quot%3BWe%20should%20use%20closed%20models%20as%20often%20as%20we%20can%2C%20and%20we%20should%20customize%20and%20use%20open%20models%20to%20build%20our%20own%20personal%2C%20our%20own%20customized%20AI%20if%20we%20must.%26quot%3B%3C%2Fp%3E%3Cdiv%3ERead%20the%20original%20article%20on%20%3Ca%20href%3D%5C%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Farena-ai-enteprises-models-trust-anastasios-angelopoulos-2026-8%5C%22%3EBusiness%20Insider%3C%2Fa%3E%3C%2Fdiv%3E%22%2C%22published%22%3A1786181761000%2C%22visual%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fi.insider.com%2F6a7631c78fcc2e955f7de87a%3Fformat%3Djpeg%22%2C%22originID%22%3A%22https%3A%2F%2Fwww.businessinsider.com%2Farena-ai-enteprises-models-trust-anastasios-angelopoulos-2026-8%22%2C%22summary%22%3A%22Arena%20CEO%20Anastasios%20Angelopoulos%20said%20companies%20are%20%26quot%3Bterrified%26quot%3B%20of%20working%20with%20frontier%20AI%20companies%20and%20China-based%20open%20models.%22%2C%22author%22%3A%22bgriffiths%40insider.com%20(Brent%20D.%20Griffiths)%22%2C%22engagement%22%3A9%2C%22canonicalUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22cdnAmpUrl%22%3A%22%22%2C%22